      "reasoning": "The learner needs a quick diagnostic before solving; the negative coefficient of $x$ is a likely sign-slip point. Ask them to identify the coefficients, focusing on the sign of $b$. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"(-5)**2 - 4*5*1\") -> 5]",
